cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "mef3io-coregistration: alignment of two MEF 3.0 (Multiscale Electrophysiology Format) recordings captured on independent, drifting clocks"
abstract: "mef3io-coregistration aligns two MEF 3.0 (Multiscale Electrophysiology Format) recordings of the same subject that were captured on independent, drifting clocks, such as a clinical EEG system and an implanted or research system. It estimates the clock offset from the signals in three stages (a gross offset over the whole recording, sample-accurate anchors, and the drift in between), saves a monotone clock map with its provenance and quality checks as JSON, and reads either recording, or both as one, on the reference clock. It is built on mef3io."
message: "If you use mef3io-coregistration in research, please cite it."
